for cutting off the part once the part has been fully machined or for machining it on another spindle.\n    TurningProfile: The turning profile strategy is used for both roughing and finishing of the part using general turning tools.\n    TurningProfileGroove: The turning groove strategy is used for both roughing and finishing of the part using groove tools.\n    TurningStockTransfer: The turning stock transfer strategy is intended for automatic stock transfer between the two spindles. No toolpath is associated with this strategy.\n        The post is responsible for outputting the desired NC code.\n    TurningThread: This strategy is used for turning threads. Both cylindrical and conical threads are supported.\n        The CNC control must have built-in support for synchronizing the spindle and feed.\n    SteepAndShallow: A 3D finishing strategy that uses Contour passes for steep areas and Parallel or Scallop passes for\n        shallow areas.\n    Flow: A 3D finishing strategy which follows the isocurves of a surface to machine parts with curved surfaces.\n        Flow is a 3-Axis toolpath by default but can be used in multi-axis modes.\n    Flow2: A 3D finishing strategy which follows the isocurves of a surface to machine parts with curved surfaces.\n        Flow is a 3-Axis toolpath by default but can be used in multi-axis modes.\n    RotaryFinishing: A multi-axis machining strategy that lets you machine along and around a rotating axis.\n        Rotary Finishing can be used for parts that are machined most efficiently when utilizing the 4th Machine Axis.\n    Chamfer2D: A 2D machining strategy that machines along contours creating a chamfered surface.\n    Morph: A 3D finishing strategy for machining shallow areas between selected contours with a consistent cutting direction.\n    MultiAxisContour: A multi-axis strategy for machining with the tip of the tool along a given contact curve.\n    MultiAxisMorph: A multi-axis strategy for machining shallow areas between selected contours with a consistent cutting direction.\n    RestFinishing: A finishing operation to machine any remaining stock left from previous operations.\n    Swarf: A multi-axis strategy for machining with the side of the tool.\n    SurfaceInspection: A strategy for the inspection of geometry using probe.\n    ManualInspection: Manual inspection.\n    ProbeWCS: Probe WCS operation\n    ProbeGeometry: Probe Geometry operation\n    PartAlignment: Part alignment.\n    PathMeasure: A surface inspection measurement with a results folder.\n    ManualMeasure: Recorded results of a manual inspection.\n",
